  "goodToKnow": "Das Fachwerk is half-timbering: a wooden frame whose panels (Fächer) are filled with wattle and daub or brick. Fachwerkhäuser shape towns such as Quedlinburg, Goslar, Celle and Wernigerode, linked by the Deutsche Fachwerkstraße, a 3,000-km tourist route. In engineering, ein Fachwerk is also a truss, as in bridges. It has no plural."
